From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:32:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 233/294] gallium/pvr: confirm our geometry-only kick still
 hangs; reference SIZEINFO values do not help

Round-twenty checks against the round-19 A/B baseline (Vulkan geometry-only reaches "TA finished",
our lone geometry kick times out):

- our geometry-only submission was retested on the latest build: still "Kick TA" then DM2 timeout;
- the TA state block's SIZEINFO words were patched to the reference's captured values
  (SIZEINFO1=0x01000000, SIZEINFO2=0x00804000; PVR_PROBE_TA_SIZEINFO) - still times out, so those
  values are not what the geometry kick needs.

So the difference is in memory our geometry command points at, not in the fields compared so far.
Verification: probe ALL PASS under the shim.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
index 2d258c28..17d3ef7d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
@@ -1131,6 +1131,16 @@ real_job_done:
                            } else {
                               const uint32_t *cw = (const uint32_t *)rctl.map;
 
+                              /* Round-20 experiment: the reference's SIZEINFO words (captured)
+                               * are non-zero where ours are zero because our shader uses no
+                               * varyings; test whether the TA kick requires them. */
+                              if (getenv("PVR_PROBE_TA_SIZEINFO")) {
+                                 uint32_t *aw = (uint32_t *)pbo.map;
+
+                                 aw[7] = 0x01000000u;
+                                 aw[8] = 0x00804000u;
+                                 printf("hwrt:          TA SIZEINFO patched to reference values\n");
+                              }
                               if (getenv("PVR_DUMP_TA")) {
                                  const uint32_t *aw = (const uint32_t *)pbo.map;
                                  printf("OURTA: TA block %u words:", pvr_csb_size(&block) / 4);
